{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5abvb6arntdwbtqo25harpf7t3v2d6fgpzaweqoomw5a2auci54q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01KfqG12rzpZLLxrNqAqERA8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-hjj0zf/translation/ERRORS.md","content":"# Phase A.2 — Error / rejection surface table\n\nMechanical grep of `c_src/src/driver.c` for every rejection mechanism:\n\n```\n$ grep -n 'return\\|assert\\|NULL\\|errno\\|exit\\|abort\\|-1\\|if (' c_src/src/driver.c\n30:    if (line != NULL)\n39:    printLine(data);        <- reads UNINITIALIZED `char *data`\n51:    if (useGood)\n```\n\nFindings:\n\n* **0** `return <errorcode>` statements — every function returns `void`.\n* **0** `assert`, `abort`, `exit`, `errno`, error enums, error macros\n  (`RETURN_ERROR` etc.), or numeric sentinels.\n* **1** explicit null check: `printLine`'s `if (line != NULL)`.\n* **0** range / min / max / size constants (no arrays, no lengths, no counts).\n* **1** implicit \"rejection-ish\" branch: `driver`'s `if (useGood)` zero-test.\n* **1** latent memory-safety defect: `bad()` passes an **uninitialized**\n  `char *` to `printLine` (CWE-457 / CWE-824). This is the intentional defect of\n  the sample and is preserved, not fixed.\n\nSo the \"error surface\" of this library is a *rejection-by-silence* surface: the\nonly way the C rejects an input is `printLine` silently doing nothing for\n`NULL`. Every row below is therefore expressed in terms of the observable\nside effect (bytes written to `stdout`) and the fact that the call returns\nnormally rather than trapping.\n\n| #  | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | test | ✅ |\n|----|----------|---------------------------------------------|-------------------|------|----|\n| E1 | `printLine` | `line == NULL` (literal null pointer across FFI) | takes the false branch, writes **0 bytes**, returns normally | `err_e1_print_line_null` | [x] |\n| E2 | `printLine` | `line` points at a lone `'\\0'` (empty C string — zero \"length\") | non-null ⇒ `printf(\"%s\\n\",\"\")` ⇒ writes exactly `\"\\n\"` | `err_e2_print_line_empty` | [x] |\n| E3 | `printLine` | `line` points at a string with **no** NUL inside the caller's intended length, i.e. the terminator is the only length bound (oversized length) — 1 MiB of `'A'` + NUL | writes 1 MiB of `'A'` + `\"\\n\"`; no truncation, no length cap | `err_e3_print_line_oversized` | [x] |\n| E4 | `printLine` | `line` contains embedded NUL after the first byte(s) — bytes past the NUL must be dropped | writes only up to (not incl.) the first NUL, then `\"\\n\"` | `err_e4_print_line_embedded_nul` | [x] |\n| E5 | `printLine` | `line` contains `%` / `%s` / `%n` format characters (data is passed as the *argument*, not the format) | `%` chars are emitted literally; **no** format-string interpretation | `err_e5_print_line_percent` | [x] |\n| E6 | `printLine` | `line` contains non-UTF-8 / high bytes `0x80..0xFF` (invalid Unicode is a valid C string) | bytes copied through verbatim | `err_e6_print_line_invalid_utf8` | [x] |\n| E7 | `driver` | `useGood == 0` (the \"false\" value ⇒ takes the defective `bad()` path) | calls `bad()`, which reads an uninitialized stack slot; returns normally | `err_e7_driver_zero` | [x] |\n| E8 | `driver` | `useGood` is a value with **no valid enum/bool variant**: `-1`, `2`, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`, `0x100`, `0xFFFF_FF00u32 as i32` — C tests truthiness, so *every* non-zero int is \"good\" | any non-zero ⇒ `good()` ⇒ `\"string\\n\"`; only exactly `0` ⇒ `bad()` | `err_e8_driver_out_of_range_enum` | [x] |\n| E9 | `driver` | `useGood` non-zero only in the **high** bytes (e.g. `0x1_0000_0000i64` truncated to `int` ⇒ `0`) — verifies the 32-bit truncation of the ABI parameter, i.e. one step past the 32-bit range | the callee sees only `%edi`; `0x100000000` truncates to `0` ⇒ `bad()` path | `err_e9_driver_int_truncation` | [x] |\n| E10 | `bad` | called directly with no arguments — the uninitialized read itself (CWE-457). The read is of the caller's stale stack at a fixed frame offset, so it must not trap and must yield the *same* bytes as the C for the same caller stack | returns normally; prints whatever the stale slot points at (`+ \"\\n\"`), or nothing if that slot happens to be `NULL` | `err_e10_bad_uninitialized_read` | [x] |\n| E11 | `good` | called directly — no invalid input is possible (no parameters); included so every entry point has an error-surface row | prints `\"string\\n\"`, returns normally | `err_e11_good_no_args` | [x] |\n\n## Generic FFI boundary cases (required even though not in the C source)\n\n| #  | case | expected | test | ✅ |\n|----|------|----------|------|----|\n| G1 | null pointer to `printLine` | silent no-op (= E1) | `err_e1_print_line_null` | [x] |\n| G2 | zero length (empty string) to `printLine` | `\"\\n\"` (= E2) | `err_e2_print_line_empty` | [x] |\n| G3 | oversized length to `printLine` (1 MiB) | full passthrough (= E3) | `err_e3_print_line_oversized` | [x] |\n| G4 | out-of-range enum int to `driver` (no valid variant) | truthiness only (= E8) | `err_e8_driver_out_of_range_enum` | [x] |\n| G5 | one step past the documented range for `driver` (`0-1` ⇒ `-1`, and `1+1` ⇒ `2`) | both non-zero ⇒ `good()` | `err_e8_driver_out_of_range_enum` | [x] |\n| G6 | repeated / interleaved calls — no hidden global state may drift | Nth call identical to 1st | `err_g6_no_hidden_state` | [x] |\n\n**Note on E10:** the C behaviour here is Undefined Behaviour, and it is\n*caller-dependent* (it is whatever 8 bytes are 16 bytes below the caller's stack\npointer at the call site). The Rust translation reproduces it exactly by using a\nnaked function with the identical prologue and the identical `-0x8(%rbp)` load,\nso that both `.so`s read the *same address* with the *same* stale contents and\ntherefore print the *same* bytes. `err_e10_bad_uninitialized_read` asserts that\nbyte equa