no_mangle] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn driver` | OK |\n\n**Missing from Rust: none.** The symbol diff is empty in both directions (modulo\nthe loader boilerplate and the `rust_*`/`_R*` runtime hooks a cdylib always\ncarries). No module of the C source was skipped; no stubs or `unimplemented!()`\nexist in the translation.\n\nAutomated as `tests/symbols.rs`:\n\n| test | checks |\n|------|--------|\n| `symbol_parity_c_subset_of_rust` | every C export exists in the Rust `.so` (the diff must be empty) |\n| `symbol_surface_is_exactly_the_four_functions` | the C surface is exactly those four, and the Rust adds nothing that looks like API |\n| `rust_so_has_no_unresolved_symbols` | `ldd -r` reports no undefined symbol |\n| `both_import_the_same_stdio_routine` | both `.so`s import `puts` — gcc lowers `printf(\"%s\\n\", …)` to `puts`, so the Rust must call the same routine |\n| `link_configuration_matches_c` | neither `.so` uses `BIND_NOW` (see below) |\n| `asm_frame_layout_matches_c` | the normalised instruction stream of all four functions is identical to gcc's |\n| `all_symbols_resolve_via_dlsym` | all four are reachable through `dlsym` |\n| `test_harness_runs_single_threaded` | guards the fd-1 capture mechanism |\n\n## Non-symbol ABI surface that also had to match\n\nSymbol parity was necessary but *not* sufficient. Two link/codegen properties\nturned out to be observable, because `bad()` reproduces the original's CWE-457\nread of an uninitialised local and therefore prints whatever bytes happen to sit\njust below its frame:\n\n1. **Frame layout.** `bad()`'s indeterminate slot is at `entry_rsp - 16`, and what\n   it contains is decided by the frame sizes and local spills of `driver`,\n   `good` and `printLine`. Idiomatic Rust codegen puts different things there,\n   so all four bodies are emitted as `naked` functions reproducing gcc's `-O0`\n   output (see `src/lib.rs`). `asm_frame_layout_matches_c` pins this.\n2. **Lazy vs eager PLT binding.** `rustc` defaults to `-z now`; `gcc` (as invoked\n   by `c_src/CMakeLists.txt`) does not. With `-z now` the dynamic linker's\n   `_dl_runtime_resolve` never runs, and that routine's stack residue is exactly\n   what `driver(0)` observes. `build.rs` therefore requests `-Wl,-z,lazy`;\n   `link_configuration_matches_c` pins this.\n\n## Feature combinations\n\n`translation/Cargo.toml` declares **no `[features]` table**, therefore the only\npossible build configurations are:\n\n| combo | command |\n|-------|---------|\n| default (= empty feature set) | `cargo test` |\n| `--no-default-features`       | `cargo test --no-default-features` |\n| `--all-features`              | `cargo test --all-features` |\n\nAll three select identical code, but all three are still exercised — together\nwith both the `dev` and `release` profiles — by `./verify.sh`, which derives the\ncombination list from `Cargo.toml` rather than hard-coding it.","originalFile":"# Phase A.1 — Symbol surface (`nm -D`)\n\n## Source inventory\n\n`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` builds exactly one translation unit into `libdriver.so`:\n\n```\nadd_library(driver SHARED src/driver.c)\n```\n\nHeaders: `c_src/include/driver.h` (declares only `void driver(int useGood);`).\n\n`c_src/src/driver.c` defines four **non-static, default-visibility** functions:\n\n| C definition            | header-declared? |\n|-------------------------|------------------|\n| `void printLine(const char *line)` | no (still exported) |\n| `void bad(void)`        | no (still exported) |\n| `void good(void)`       | no (still exported) |\n| `void driver(int useGood)` | yes |\n\nThere is no second module, no macro-generated symbol family, no `#ifdef`\ncompile-time configuration, and no data symbol. The whole library is 59 lines.\n\n## `nm -D --defined-only` comparison\n\nC — `c_src/build/libdriver.so`:\n\n```\n000000000000115b T bad\n0000000000001194 T driver\n0000000000001172 T good\n0000000000001139 T printLine\n```\n\nRust — `translation/target/release/libdriver.so`:\n\n```\n00000000000117b0 T bad\n00000000000117c0 T driver\n00000000000117e0 T good\n00000000000117f0 T printLine\n```\n\n## Parity table\n\n| # | symbol      | type | in C `.so` | in Rust `.so` | Rust implementation | status |\n|---|-------------|------|-----------|---------------|---------------------|--------|\n| 1 | `printLine` | `T` (func) | yes | yes | `src/lib.rs` `#[no_mangle] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn printLine` | OK |\n| 2 | `bad`       | `T` (func) | yes | yes | `src/lib.rs` `#[no_mangle] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn bad` (naked, mirrors the C frame layout) | OK |\n| 3 | `good`      | `T` (func) | yes | yes | `src/lib.rs` `#[no_mangle] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn good` | OK |\n| 4 | `driver`    | `T` (func) | yes | yes | `src/lib.rs` `#[no_mangle] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn driver` | OK |\n\n**Missing from Rust: none.** No module of the C source was skipped; no stubs or\n`unimplemented!()` exist in the translation.\n\n## Undefined (imported) symbols\n\nC `.so` imports from libc: `printf` (plus the usual `__cxa_finalize`,\n`_ITM_*`/`__gmon_start__` weak loader symbols).\n\nRust `.so` imports `printf` from libc as well (the translation deliberately\ncalls libc `printf` instead of Rust `println!`, so stdout buffering and\ninterleaving are byte-identical). Everything else the Rust `.so` needs is\nstatically linked from `libstd`/`compiler_builtins`; there are **0 missing or\nunresolvable non-libc undefined symbols** (verified by `ldd -r`, see\n`tests/symbols.rs::rust_so_has_no_unresolved_symbols`).\n\n## Feature combinations\n\n`translation/Cargo.toml` declares **no `[features]` table**, therefore the only\npossible build configurations are:\n\n| combo | command |\n|-------|---------|\n| default (= empty feature set) | `cargo test` |\n| `--no-default-features`       | `cargo test --no-default-features` |\n| `--all-features`              | `cargo test --all-features` |\n\nAll three are identical code paths, but all three are still exercised by\n`scratch/check_features.sh` for completeness.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":47,"oldLines":13,"newStart":47,"newLines":61,"lines":[" | # | symbol      | type | in C `.so` | in Rust `.so` | Rust implementation | status |"," |---|-------------|------|-----------|---------------|---------------------|--------|"," | 1 | `printLine` | `T` (func) | yes | yes | `src/lib.rs` `#[no_mangle] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn printLine` | OK |","-| 2 | `bad`       | `T` (func) | yes | yes | `src/lib.rs` `#[no_mangle] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn bad` (naked, mirrors the C frame layout) | OK |","+| 2 | `bad`       | `T` (func) | yes | yes | `src/lib.rs` `#[no_mangle] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn bad` | OK |"," | 3 | `good`      | `T` (func) | yes | yes | `src/lib.rs` `#[no_mangle] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn good` | OK |"," | 4 | `driver`    | `T` (func) | yes | yes | `src/lib.rs` `#[no_mangle] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn driver` | OK |"," ","-**Missing from Rust: none.** No module of the C source was skipped; no stubs or","-`unimplemented!()` exist in the translation.","+**Missing from Rust: none.** The symbol diff is empty in both directions (modulo","+the loader boilerplate and the `rust_*`/`_R*` runtime hooks a cdylib always","+carries). No module of the C source was skipped; no stubs or `unimplemented!()`","+exist in the translation."," ","+Automated as `tests/symbols.rs`:","+","+| test | checks |","+|------|--------|","+| `symbol_parity_c_subset_of_rust` | every C export exists in the Rust `.so` (the diff must be empty) |","+| `symbol_surface_is_exactly_the_four_functions` | the C surface is exactly those four, and the Rust adds nothing that looks like API |","+| `rust_so_has_no_unresolved_symbols` | `ldd -r` reports no undefined symbol |","+| `both_import_the_same_stdio_routine` | both `.so`s import `puts` — gcc lowers `printf(\"%s\\n\", …)` to `puts`, so the Rust must call the same routine |","+| `link_configuration_matches_c` | neither `.so` uses `BIND_NOW` (see below) |","+| `asm_frame_layout_matches_c` | the no