e call returns","-normally rather than trapping.","+So this library's error surface is a *rejection-by-silence* surface. Each row","+below therefore states the exact observable result: the bytes written to stdout","+**and** how the call terminates (clean return vs. fatal signal). Rows that can","+fault are asserted in a forked child so that \"both crashed the same way\" is","+distinguished from \"both returned normally\" — never merely \"both failed","+somehow\"."," ","-| #  | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | test | ✅ |","-|----|----------|---------------------------------------------|-------------------|------|----|","-| E1 | `printLine` | `line == NULL` (literal null pointer across FFI) | takes the false branch, writes **0 bytes**, returns normally | `err_e1_print_line_null` | [x] |","-| E2 | `printLine` | `line` points at a lone `'\\0'` (empty C string — zero \"length\") | non-null ⇒ `printf(\"%s\\n\",\"\")` ⇒ writes exactly `\"\\n\"` | `err_e2_print_line_empty` | [x] |","-| E3 | `printLine` | `line` points at a string with **no** NUL inside the caller's intended length, i.e. the terminator is the only length bound (oversized length) — 1 MiB of `'A'` + NUL | writes 1 MiB of `'A'` + `\"\\n\"`; no truncation, no length cap | `err_e3_print_line_oversized` | [x] |","-| E4 | `printLine` | `line` contains embedded NUL after the first byte(s) — bytes past the NUL must be dropped | writes only up to (not incl.) the first NUL, then `\"\\n\"` | `err_e4_print_line_embedded_nul` | [x] |","-| E5 | `printLine` | `line` contains `%` / `%s` / `%n` format characters (data is passed as the *argument*, not the format) | `%` chars are emitted literally; **no** format-string interpretation | `err_e5_print_line_percent` | [x] |","-| E6 | `printLine` | `line` contains non-UTF-8 / high bytes `0x80..0xFF` (invalid Unicode is a valid C string) | bytes copied through verbatim | `err_e6_print_line_invalid_utf8` | [x] |","-| E7 | `driver` | `useGood == 0` (the \"false\" value ⇒ takes the defective `bad()` path) | calls `bad()`, which reads an uninitialized stack slot; returns normally | `err_e7_driver_zero` | [x] |","-| E8 | `driver` | `useGood` is a value with **no valid enum/bool variant**: `-1`, `2`, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`, `0x100`, `0xFFFF_FF00u32 as i32` — C tests truthiness, so *every* non-zero int is \"good\" | any non-zero ⇒ `good()` ⇒ `\"string\\n\"`; only exactly `0` ⇒ `bad()` | `err_e8_driver_out_of_range_enum` | [x] |","-| E9 | `driver` | `useGood` non-zero only in the **high** bytes (e.g. `0x1_0000_0000i64` truncated to `int` ⇒ `0`) — verifies the 32-bit truncation of the ABI parameter, i.e. one step past the 32-bit range | the callee sees only `%edi`; `0x100000000` truncates to `0` ⇒ `bad()` path | `err_e9_driver_int_truncation` | [x] |","-| E10 | `bad` | called directly with no arguments — the uninitialized read itself (CWE-457). The read is of the caller's stale stack at a fixed frame offset, so it must not trap and must yield the *same* bytes as the C for the same caller stack | returns normally; prints whatever the stale slot points at (`+ \"\\n\"`), or nothing if that slot happens to be `NULL` | `err_e10_bad_uninitialized_read` | [x] |","-| E11 | `good` | called directly — no invalid input is possible (no parameters); included so every entry point has an error-surface row | prints `\"string\\n\"`, returns normally | `err_e11_good_no_args` | [x] |","+## The table"," ","-## Generic FFI boundary cases (required even though not in the C source)","+| #  | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | test (`tests/errors.rs`) | ✅ |","+|----|----------|---------------------------------------------|-------------------|--------------------------|----|","+| E1 | `printLine` | `line == NULL` (literal null pointer across FFI) | takes the false branch: **0 bytes**, `exit(0)` | `err_e1_print_line_null` | [x] |","+| E2 | `printLine` | `line` points at a lone `'\\0'` (empty string = \"zero length\") | non-null ⇒ `puts(\"\")` ⇒ exactly `\"\\n\"` | `err_e2_print_line_empty` | [x] |","+| E3 | `printLine` | oversized length — 1 MiB of `'A'`; the NUL terminator is the *only* bound, there is no length cap | 1 MiB of `'A'` then `\"\\n\"`, no truncation | `err_e3_print_line_oversized` | [x] |","+| E4 | `printLine` | embedded NUL: bytes after the first NUL must be dropped | output stops at (excluding) the first NUL, then `\"\\n\"` | `err_e4_print_line_embedded_nul` | [x] |","+| E5 | `printLine` | `%`, `%s`, `%n`, `%*d` … in the *data* (it is the argument, not the format) | `%` sequences emitted literally, **no** format interpretation, no `%n` write | `err_e5_print_line_percent` | [x] |","+| E6 | `printLine` | non-UTF-8 / high bytes `0x80..=0xFF` (still valid C strings) | bytes copied through verbatim | `err_e6_print_line_invalid_utf8` | [x] |","+| E7 | `driver` | `useGood == 0` — selects the defective `bad()` branch | calls `bad()`, which reads an indeterminate slot; here `\"\\n\"` + `exit(0)`, and `SIGSEGV` from a dirtied stack | `err_e7_driver_zero` | [x] |","+| E8 | `driver` | `useGood` with **no valid enum/bool variant**: `-1`, `2`, `3`, `-2`, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`, `0x100`, `0xFFFF`, `0xFFFFFF00u32 as i32`, … | C tests plain truthiness, so *every* non-zero int ⇒ `good()` ⇒ `\"string\\n\"`; only exactly `0` ⇒ `bad()` | `err_e8_driver_out_of_range_enum` | [x] |","+| E9 | `driver` | a value one step past the 32-bit range: the symbol called through a `fn(u64)` pointer with `0x1_0000_0000`, `0x1_0000_0001`, `0xFFFFFFFF_00000000` | the callee reads only `%edi`, so these truncate to `0`, `1`, `0` and pick `bad`, `good`, `bad` | `err_e9_driver_int_truncation` | [x] |","+| E10 | `bad` | the uninitialised read itself (CWE-457), from a clean stack and from stacks pre-dirtied with 4 fill patterns × 3 recursion depths | returns normally printing the stale bytes when the slot is a readable pointer; `SIGSEGV` when it is not | `err_e10_bad_uninitialized_read` | [x] |","+| E11 | `good` | no invalid input is representable (no parameters) — included so every entry point has a row | `\"string\\n\"`, `exit(0)` | `err_e11_good_no_args` | [x] |"," ","+## Generic FFI-boundary cases (required even though not in the C source)","+"," | #  | case | expected | test | ✅ |"," |----|------|----------|------|----|","-| G1 | null pointer to `printLine` | silent no-op (= E1) | `err_e1_print_line_null` | [x] |","-| G2 | zero length (empty string) to `printLine` | `\"\\n\"` (= E2) | `err_e2_print_line_empty` | [x] |","-| G3 | oversized length to `printLine` (1 MiB) | full passthrough (= E3) | `err_e3_print_line_oversized` | [x] |","+| G1 | null pointer to `printLine` | silent no-op, clean return (= E1) | `err_e1_print_line_null` | [x] |","+| G2 | zero length (empty string) | `\"\\n\"` (= E2) | `err_e2_print_line_empty` | [x] |","+| G3 | oversized length (1 MiB) | full passthrough (= E3) | `err_e3_print_line_oversized` | [x] |"," | G4 | out-of-range enum int to `driver` (no valid variant) | truthiness only (= E8) | `err_e8_driver_out_of_range_enum` | [x] |","-| G5 | one step past the documented range for `driver` (`0-1` ⇒ `-1`, and `1+1` ⇒ `2`) | both non-zero ⇒ `good()` | `err_e8_driver_out_of_range_enum` | [x] |","-| G6 | repeated / interleaved calls — no hidden global state may drift | Nth call identical to 1st | `err_g6_no_hidden_state` | [x] |","+| G5 | one step past the documented range (`-1` and `2`) | both non-zero ⇒ `good()` | `err_e8_driver_out_of_range_enum` | [x] |","+| G6 | repeated / interleaved calls — no hidden global state may drift | the Nth call is identical to the 1st (perfectly periodic stream over 50 rounds) | `err_g6_no_hidden_state` | [x] |","+| G7 | pointer shapes: pointer to a buffer's terminating NUL (off-by-one), odd/unaligned offsets, read-only static storage | all are valid C strings and must behave | `err_extra_pointer_shapes` | [x] |","+| G8 | wild non-NULL pointers (`1`, `8`, `0x1000`, `0xdeadbeef`, top of the address space) — the C has no way to reject these | both must fault **identically** (same signal, same partial output) | `err_extra_wild_pointer` | [x] |"," ","-**Note on E10:** the C behaviour here is Undefined Behaviour, and it is","-*caller-dependent* (it is whatever 8 bytes are 16 bytes below the caller's stack","-pointer at the call site). The Rust translation reproduces it exactly by using a","-naked function with the identical prologue and the identical `-0x8(%rbp)` load,","-so that both `.so`s read the *same address* with the *same* stale contents and","-therefore print the *same* bytes. `err_e10_bad_uninitialized_read` asserts that","-byte equality, and also asserts it holds when the caller's stack is deliberately","-pre-dirtied with several different fill patterns and depths.","+## Notes","+","+**E10 / E7 and the limits of \"identical\".** The C behaviour here is Undefined","+Behaviour, and it is *caller-dependent*: the value is whatever eight bytes sit","+16 bytes below the callee's entry stack pointer. The Rust reproduces it exactly","+by matching gcc's frame layout instruction-for-instruction, so both `.so`s read","+the *same address* with the *same* stale contents. The tests confirm this is not","+vacuous: for `printLine(\"AAAA…\"); bad();` both libraries dump the same ~60 bytes","+of stale machine code from the stack, and for a dirtied stack both take SIGSEGV","+at the same point. See `SYMBOLS.md` for the two link/codegen properties this","+depends on.","+","+The differential harness itself has to be symmetric for these rows to be","+meaningful — see the module documentation in `tests/common/mod.rs`.","+","+**Mutation-tested.** Each of these rows was checked to actually *fail* when the","+translation is wrong; four deliberate regressions were injected and all were","+caught:","+","+| injected regression | caught by |","+|---------------------|-----------|","+| `bad()` replaced by a \"safe\" deterministic empty string | `cfg_c12_bad`, `cfg_c18_repeat_no_drift`, `cfg_c19_dirty_stack_matrix`, `cfg_c19b_good_then_bad_frame_aliasing` |","+| `-Wl,-z,lazy` dropped from `build.rs` (i.e. `BIND_NOW`) | `cfg_c14`, `cfg_c15`, `cfg_c16`, `cfg_c19`, `cfg_c19b`, `err_e7`, `err_e8`, `err_e9`, `link_configuration_matches_c` |","+| `printLine`'s NULL check removed | `cfg_c10_printline_null`, `err_e1_print_line_null` |","+| `driver`'s branch inverted | `cfg_c13_driver_one`, `cfg_c14_driver_zero` |"]}],"originalFile":"# Phase A.2 — Error / rejection surface table\n\nMechanical grep of `c_src/src/driver.c` for every rejection mechanism:\n\n```\n$ grep -n 'return\\|assert\\|NULL\\|errno\\|exit\\|abort\\|-1\\|if (' c_src/src/driver.c\n30:    if (line != NULL)\n39:    printLine(data);        <- reads UNINITIALIZED `char *data`\n51:    if (useGood)\n```\n\nFindings:\n\n* **0** `return <errorcode>` statements — every function returns `void`.\n* **0** `assert`, `abort`, `exit`, `errno`, error enums, error macros\n  (`RETURN_ERROR` etc.), or numeric sentinels.\n* **1** explicit null check: `printLine`'s `if (line != NULL)`.\n* **0** range / min / max / size constants (no arrays, no lengths, no counts).\n* **1** implicit \"rejection-ish\" branch: `driver`'s `if (useGood)` zero-test.\n* **1** latent memory-safety defect: `bad()` passes an **uninitialized**\n  `char *` to `printLine` (CWE-457 / CWE-824). This is the intentional defect of\n  the sample and is preserved, not fixed.\n\nSo the \"error surface\" of this library is a *rejection-by-silence* surface: the\nonly way the C rejects an input is `printLine` silently doing nothing for\n`NULL`. Every row below is therefore expressed in terms of the observable\nside effect (bytes written to `stdout`) and the fact that the call returns\nnormally rather than trapping.\n\n| #  | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | test | ✅ |\n|----|----------|---------------------------------------------|-------------------|------|----|\n| E1 | `printLine` | `line == NULL` (literal null pointer across FFI) | takes the false branch, writes **0 bytes**, returns normally | `err_e1_print_line_null` | [x] |\n| E2 | `printLine` | `line` points at a lone `'\\0'` (empty C string — zero \"length\") | non-null ⇒ `printf(\"%s\\n\",\"\")` ⇒ writes exactly `\"\\n\"` | `err_e2_print_line_empty` | [x] |\n| E3 | `printLine` | `line` points at a string with **no** NUL inside the caller's intended length, i.e. the terminator is the only length bound (oversized length) — 1 MiB of `'A'` + NUL | writes 1 MiB of `'A'` + `\"\\n\"`; no truncation, no length cap | `err_e3_print_line_oversized` | [x] |\n| E4 | `printLine` | `line` contains embedded NUL after the first byte(s) — bytes past the NUL must be dropped | writes only up to (not incl.) the first NUL, then `\"\\n\"` | `err_e4_print_line_embedded_nul` | [x] |\n| E5 | `printLine` | `line` contains `%` / `%s` / `%n` format characters (data is passed as the *argument*, not the format) | `%` chars are emitted literally; **no** format-string interpretation | `err_e5_print_line_percent` | [x] |\n| E6 | `printLine` | `line` contains non-UTF-8 / high bytes `0x80..0xFF` (invalid Unicode is a valid C string) | bytes copied through verbatim | `err_e6_print_line_invalid_utf8` | [x] |\n| E7 | `driver` | `useGood == 0` (the \"false\" value ⇒ takes the defective `bad()` path) | calls `bad()`, which reads an uninitialized stack slot; returns normally | `err_e7_driver_zero` | [x] |\n| E8 | `driver` | `useGood` is a value with **no valid enum/bool variant**: `-1`, `2`, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`, `0x100`, `0xFFFF_FF00u32 as i32` — C tests truthiness, so *every* non-zero int is \"good\" | any non-zero ⇒ `good()` ⇒ `\"string\\n\"`; only exactly `0` ⇒ `bad()` | `err_e8_driver_out_of_range_enum` | [x] |\n| E9 | `driver` | `useGood` non-zero only in the **high** bytes (e.g. `0x1_0000_0000i64` truncated to `int` ⇒ `0`) — verifies the 32-bit truncation of the ABI parameter, i.e. one step past the 32-bit range | the callee sees only `%edi`; `0x100000000` truncates to `0` ⇒ `bad()` path | `err_e9_driver_int_truncation` | [x] |\n| E10 | `bad` | called directly with no arguments — the uninitialized read itself (CWE-457). The read is of the caller's stale stack at a fixed frame offset, so it must not trap and must yield the *same* bytes as the C for the same caller stack | returns normally; prints whatever the stale slot points at (`+ \"\\n\"`), or nothing if that slot happens to be `NULL` | `err_e10_bad_uninitialized_read` | [x] |\n| E11 | `good` | called directly — no invalid input is possible (no parameters); included so every entry point has an error-surface row | prints `\"string\\n\"`, returns normally | `err_e11_good_no_args` | [x] |\n\n## Generic FFI boundary cases (required even though not in the C source)\n\n| #  | case | expected | test | ✅ |\n|----|------|----------|------|----|\n| G1 | null pointer to `printLine` | silent no-op (= E1) | `err_e1_print_line_null` | [x] |\n| G2 | zero length (empty string) to `printLine` | `\"\\n\"` (= E2) | `err_e2_print_line_empty` | [x] |\n| G3 | oversized length to `printLine` (1 MiB) | full passthrough (= E3) | `err_e3_print_line_oversized` | [x] |\n| G4 | out-of-range enum int to `driver` (no valid variant) | truthiness only (= E8) | `err_e8_driver_out_of_range_enum` | [x] |\n| G5 | one step past the documented range for `driver` (`0-1` ⇒ `-1`, and `1+1` ⇒ `2`) | both non-zero ⇒ `good()` | `err_e8_driver_out_of_range_enum` | [x] |\n| G6 | repeated / interleaved calls — no hidden global state may drift | Nth call identical to 1st | `err_g6_no_hidden_state` | [x] |\n\n**Note on E10:** the C behaviour here is Undefined Behaviour, and it is\n*caller-dependent* (it is whatever 8 bytes are 16 bytes below the caller's stack\npointer at the call site). The Rust translation reproduces it exactly by using a\nnaked function with the identical prologue and the identical `-0x8(%rbp)` load,\nso that both `.so`s read the *same address* with the *same* stale contents and\ntherefore print the *same* bytes. `err_e10_bad_uninitialized_read` asserts that\nbyte equality, and also asserts it holds when the caller's stack is deliberately\npre-dirtied with several different fill patterns and depths.\n","userModified":false}}
