{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_d5qkhscxnzongueecuomupf7sqsk5yq2keeediinsid547rphexa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass, and I found and fixed two real divergences.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src` is a 59-line CWE-457 sample exporting four symbols: `printLine`, `bad`, `good`, `driver`. `bad()` deliberately passes an **uninitialized** `char *` to `printLine`.\n\n## Phase A — artifacts (`translation/`)\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | all 4 `nm -D` exports; diff C↔Rust is **empty**; imports (`puts`), and the non-symbol ABI properties that also had to match |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 11 rejection rows (E1–E11) + 8 generic FFI rows (G1–G8), derived by grepping every `if`/`NULL`/`return`/`assert` in the C |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 21 valid-input rows (C1–C20 + C19b) over the axes the C actually branches on |\n\n## Two real divergences found and fixed\n\n**1. `bad()` didn't reproduce the indeterminate read.** The original translation substituted a deterministic empty string. The C's actual behaviour depends on its *frame layout*, and diverged immediately:\n\n- `good(); bad();` → C prints `string\\nstring\\n` (gcc spills the literal into exactly the slot `bad` reads); Rust printed `string\\n\\n`.\n- With a dirtied caller stack the C takes **SIGSEGV**; the Rust returned cleanly.\n\nFix: emit all four bodies as `naked` functions reproducing gcc `-O0`'s instruction streams (also switching `printf(\"%s\\n\",…)` → `puts`, which is what gcc actually emits). The disassembly is now instruction-for-instruction identical, pinned by a test.\n\n**2. The Rust `.so` was linked `-z now`; the C's is lazily bound.** With `BIND_NOW` the loader's `_dl_runtime_resolve` never runs — and its stack residue is exactly what `driver(0)` reads. Fixed in `build.rs` (`-Wl,-z,lazy`).\n\nBoth now match byte-for-byte, including cases where both libraries dump the *same ~60 bytes of stale machine code* off the stack, and cases where both SIGSEGV.\n\n## Test suite (`tests/`, all via `libloading` on both `.so`s)\n\n- `configs.rs` (21), `errors.rs` (14), `symbols.rs` (8), `probe_ub.rs` (diagnostic).\n- Crash-capable paths run in `fork()`ed children comparing **bytes + termination signal**, so \"both SIGSEGV'd identically\" is a real assertion.\n- The harness itself had to be made symmetric (one monomorphization, one call site, fixed-width temp names) — asymmetry there caused a false failure in `--release`.\n\n## Mutation-tested (the checks aren't vacuous)\n\n| injected regression | caught? |\n|---|---|\n| \"safe\" deterministic `bad()` | ✅ 4 tests, both profiles |\n| `BIND_NOW` restored | ✅ 9 tests, both profiles |\n| `printLine`'s NULL check removed | ✅ 2 tests |\n| `driver`'s branch inverted | ✅ 2 tests |\n\n## Phase D gate\n\n`./verify.sh` sweeps every feature combination (`Cargo.toml` declares none, so default / `--no-default-features` / `--all-features`, derived from the manifest) × `dev`/`release`: **ALL COMBINATIONS PASSED**, 30 ok results, 0 failures, exit 0. Symbol diff empty for both profiles. `c_src/` was not modified (only the generated `build/` directory added).\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: fidelity on the `bad()` path relies on matching `gcc -O0` codegen, which is what `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` produces (it sets no optimization flags). If the C were rebuilt at `-O2`, gcc could compile that undefined behaviour differently and the layout-exact translation would need re-checking; `asm_frame_layout_matches_c` is the test that would catch it."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1033,"cache_read_input_tokens":213679,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1033,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e25d0245-0da3-449f-ad2c-b94e24aa7eb9","uuid":"34